/**
 * @defgroup installation Installation Guide
 * @{
 * @brief Installation and setup instructions for the ArgusAI system
 *
 * This guide provides detailed instructions for installing and setting up the
 * ArgusAI system on your local machine or server.
 *
 * @section requirements System Requirements
 *
 * @subsection hardware Hardware Requirements
 * - CPU: 4+ cores recommended
 * - RAM: 8GB minimum, 16GB recommended
 * - GPU: NVIDIA GPU with CUDA support (optional but recommended)
 * - Storage: 10GB free space minimum
 *
 * @subsection software Software Requirements
 * - Python 3.8 or higher
 * - Node.js 16 or higher
 * - CUDA Toolkit 11.0+ (for GPU support)
 * - Git
 *
 * @section installation Installation Steps
 *
 * @subsection backend_install Backend Installation
 * 1. Clone the repository:
 * @code{.bash}
 * git clone https://github.com/yourusername/argusai.git
 * cd argusai
 * @endcode
 *
 * 2. Create and activate a virtual environment:
 * @code{.bash}
 * python -m venv venv
 * source venv/bin/activate  # Linux/Mac
 * venv\Scripts\activate     # Windows
 * @endcode
 *
 * 3. Install Python dependencies:
 * @code{.bash}
 * pip install -r backend/requirements.txt
 * @endcode
 *
 * @subsection frontend_install Frontend Installation
 * 1. Navigate to the frontend directory:
 * @code{.bash}
 * cd frontend
 * @endcode
 *
 * 2. Install Node.js dependencies:
 * @code{.bash}
 * npm install
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section configuration Configuration
 *
 * @subsection backend_config Backend Configuration
 * 1. Create a `.env` file in the backend directory:
 * @code{.bash}
 * cp .env.example .env
 * @endcode
 *
 * 2. Configure the following environment variables:
 * - `MODEL_PATH`: Path to YOLO model files
 * - `PORT`: Backend server port (default: 8000)
 * - `GPU_ENABLED`: Enable GPU support (true/false)
 *
 * @subsection frontend_config Frontend Configuration
 * 1. Create a `.env` file in the frontend directory:
 * @code{.bash}
 * cp .env.example .env
 * @endcode
 *
 * 2. Configure the following environment variables:
 * - `VITE_API_URL`: Backend API URL
 * - `VITE_APP_TITLE`: Application title
 *
 * @section running Running the Application
 *
 * @subsection backend_run Running the Backend
 * 1. Activate the virtual environment:
 * @code{.bash}
 * source venv/bin/activate  # Linux/Mac
 * venv\Scripts\activate     # Windows
 * @endcode
 *
 * 2. Start the backend server:
 * @code{.bash}
 * cd backend
 * python main.py
 * @endcode
 *
 * @subsection frontend_run Running the Frontend
 * 1. Start the development server:
 * @code{.bash}
 * cd frontend
 * npm run dev
 * @endcode
 *
 * 2. Access the application at http://localhost:5173
 *
 * @section troubleshooting Troubleshooting
 *
 * @subsection common_issues Common Issues
 * 1. CUDA/GPU Issues
 *    - Ensure CUDA Toolkit is properly installed
 *    - Verify GPU drivers are up to date
 *    - Check CUDA version compatibility
 *
 * 2. Port Conflicts
 *    - Change the port in configuration if default ports are in use
 *    - Check for running processes on required ports
 *
 * 3. Model Loading Issues
 *    - Verify model files are in the correct location
 *    - Check model file permissions
 *    - Ensure sufficient disk space
 *
 * @subsection getting_help Getting Help
 * If you encounter issues not covered in this guide:
 * 1. Check the GitHub Issues page
 * 2. Review the documentation
 * 3. Contact the development team
 *
 * @see backend
 * @see frontend
 * @}
 */ 